{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Hear my voice.</b> For they were separating from him from marital relations, because he had killed Cain and Tuval-Cain his son — for Lemech was blind and Tuval-Cain would guide him, and he saw Cain and it seemed to him like an animal, and he said to his father to draw the bow, and he killed him; and once he knew that it was Cain his forefather, he struck palm against palm and clapped his son between them and killed him. And his wives were separating from him, and he was placating them:" "<b>Hear my voice.</b> To hearken to me for marital relations. 'The man whom I killed — was it for my wound that he was killed? Did I wound him intentionally, that the wound should be called by my name? And the child whom I killed — was it for my bruise that he was killed?' — that is, on account of my bruise? — in astonishment: 'But I am unintentional, not intentional — this is not my wound and this is not my bruise!'" "<b>Wound.</b> A sword-stroke or arrow; מקא\"דורה בְּלַעַ\"ז."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "the la'az is Old French esquadure or similar, denoting a blade- or arrow-wound"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:02.505146111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}